Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:04.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,Before a network service ships, someone should find out exactly where it breaks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.54,0:00:18.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,AETHER-NIM is a crash-test lab for fiber networks. It starts healthy: seventeen nodes, twenty links, five demand pairs, held together by one number, algebraic connectivity: five point three seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.19,0:00:27.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,Now the gap. Dashboards show that something broke. Meetings decide what to do next. Hours pass. But the answer is already inside the graph.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.14,0:00:37.73,Cap,,0,0,0,,So we break it, for real. A bridge link fails. Lambda two collapses to exactly zero. Two islands form. Throughput craters. Measured, not imagined.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.73,0:00:53.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,Diagnosis runs two sources at once. A structured incident report goes to NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius Token Factory. And at the exact same moment, the twin calls the Tavily Search API for live fiber-outage context from the real web.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.18,0:01:02.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,Nemotron returns root causes, a ranked repair plan, risks and confidence, as strict JSON. And you can see the live citations on screen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.47,0:01:13.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,Now the rule. AI proposes. The engine disposes. Every proposed action is validated against the live graph, planned by a deterministic optimizer, with rollback armed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.42,0:01:25.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,The repair executes. A separate verifier recomputes every metric from scratch: success. One component. Five out of five demand pairs. Throughput restored. In seconds, not hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.99,0:01:35.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,Every claim on this screen was measured, repaired and proven. AETHER-NIM. Trust, but verify, as software. Live demo and code below.
